            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0169" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/>

                <head>J. H. Vries</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 7, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Illustrious Excellency</hi>: I have the honor
                    of sending you a copy of my letter to Mrs. Lincoln and the illustrious nation
                    whose destinies are intrusted to your hands. You will see in it the faithful
                    expression of my sentiments for the great statesman Abraham Lincoln. You will
                    find, at the same time, an antidote to the plague which threatens America by the
                    crime of Dr. Blackburn.</p>
                <p>I do not doubt but the papers will make known this remedy by publication, and
                    thus snatch from certain death thousands of victims, if the dreadful plague
                    should break out.</p>
                <p>May God give you the light to lead the great nation of the United States to its
                    highest destiny, is my most cordial wish for you, whom Providence has called to
                    the eminent post of President.</p>
                <p>Deign to accept the humble homage of the distinguished sentiments with which I
                    have the honor to be your excellency’s very humble and most obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. H. VRIES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">President</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
